  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Systematic audit against the current schema.org vocabulary: closed hundreds of missing-property gaps across the library (CreativeWork, Organization, Place, Product, Offer, Person, JobPosting, Event, and many more), added several new supporting types (Grant, InteractionCounter, Certification, Credential, MemberProgram, ShippingService, Occupation), and fixed a handful of real bugs found along the way - Thing.SubjectOf/Action.Location type gaps, IBook.Isbn mismatch, Person.Height/Sponsor/Address using the wrong backing field or type, and Vehicle properties serializing under the wrong or legacy JSON keys (including a copy-paste bug on VehicleIdentificationNumber). Also fixed: CourseInstance.CourseMode serializing under the wrong key (\"coursePrerequisites\"), OrderItem having three different properties all serialize under the same \"orderItemNumber\" key, Blog.BlogPost missing its JsonProperty attribute entirely, Order/OrderItem's OrderStatus enum serializing as a number instead of its name, ChooseAction.Option under \"option\" instead of \"actionOption\", BedDetails.typeOfBed sharing NumberOfBeds's key, Audience's geographic area under a key (\"administrativeArea\") that was never a valid schema.org property name, NutritionInformation.SugarContent serializing under \"occupancy\", and TravelAction.Distance being unserializable (no access modifier, no JsonProperty). This audit is now complete: every class in the library matching a current schema.org type implements all of that type's non-superseded properties. Additionally, Person/Organization/Place.Address (and IPlace.Address/Addresses) now accept Text in addition to PostalAddress, matching schema.org's documented union; Organization/Place.Addresses is now List<object> instead of List<PostalAddress> to support this. See ChangeLog.md for full details.",
